{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1786480251,"nonce":"mFgbMSQzz04N+10gULnSUjzqWEE=","target":"29ca57bf542bb3d629bd6e790175c2604620714e544e0aae00dd1867bef46dcc","message":"**What is wrong.** `internal/enrichment/domain` has **no `New…() (T, error)` constructor at all**. The only invariant enforcement is an optional `Enrichment.Validate()` that any caller may forget to call, and `CacheEntry` has no enforcement whatsoever.\n\nThis contradicts the repo's own stated rule. CONTEXT.md §5b: *\"No optional Validate() in domain. If you can construct it, it is valid.\"* And the §5 layer table: *\"Domain invariants | value objects + New…() (T, error)\"*.\n\n**The demonstration.** The zero value of `Enrichment` is fully constructible and violates **six DDL CHECKs at once**, and nothing in the type system stops it reaching a repository. `CacheEntry` is worse: `enrichment_cache_key_ck` and `enrichment_cache_exp_ck` are re-checked in `internal/enrichment/repository/cache.go` — the invariant lives in the repository rather than in the domain, which is the layering inverted.\n\n**Why it matters.** This is an invariant hole, not a behaviour defect in `Validate`. Every other domain in oto enforces construction, so this is the one place where \"if it compiles it is valid\" stops being true — and the cost is a 23514 surfacing as a 500 at write time rather than an error at construction time. It is also the shape that makes a whole package unsafe to refactor: nothing tells a future caller it must validate.\n\n**Where.** `internal/enrichment/domain/enrichment.go:159` (the optional `Validate`), `CacheEntry` in the same package, `internal/enrichment/repository/cache.go` (where the CacheEntry invariants currently live).\n\n**Pinned by** the skipped `TestBUG_EnrichmentIsConstructibleWhileInvalid` in `internal/enrichment/domain/enrichment_test.go:796`.\n\n**Done when.** `Enrichment` and `CacheEntry` are constructible only through `New…() (T, error)`, the cache invariants move from the repository into the domain, and the pin is unskipped.","files":null}]}